   146	| S140 | git-status documentation — https://git-scm.com/docs/git-status | docs | A | Git's Version 1 porcelain status format, the form a gate should parse to read worktree state | Page fetched 2026-10-28 (HTTP 200, 99,934 bytes, sha256 `903e31c527d443ab4051f7b4e0225058efd96a45d0400538f6ba19b5c9c59ad9`); anchors `Porcelain Format Version 1` and the `-z` machine-parsing paragraph | The v1 porcelain format is guaranteed not to change backwards-incompatibly and is the form a script should parse; `-z` makes the fields NUL-terminated, which is what the dirty arm reads. | mined | 2026-10-28 | on-release | corpus/lessons/round-45.md |
